Database["public"]["Tables"]. Documented `amount` as GROSS rent on both the Row
type and the Insert shape.

Files: lib/supabase/database.types.ts (modified)

THE CORE WHY
This file is hand-maintained — `supabase gen types` is explicitly forbidden in
CLAUDE.md — so a new column is invisible to TypeScript until it is added here,
and the style guide warns that a type assertion around a Supabase query usually
means this file is stale rather than that the cast is right.

The invariants live on the type, not only in the migration, because this is
what a developer sees at the call site: `amount` is gross rent, fee columns are
GST-inclusive (residential rent is input-taxed, so no GST credit is claimable
and the GST-inclusive figure is the deductible one), and other_outgoings is
reconciliation-only and never a deduction.

`extracted` is typed Record<string, unknown> | null, matching the existing
convention used by loan_statements and staged_receipts. There is no exported
Json type in this file — an initial draft used one and would not have compiled.

