VERIFICATION DEBT
The type-check proves the shape compiles; it does not prove the typed client
can write these columns at runtime (a type that compiles is not proof the
column exists — the style guide says so explicitly). That runtime proof comes
in task 4, which inserts a statement_path row through the typed client in the
deletion harness.
